  "$id": "design-lab/project-list/v1",
  "title": "Project roll-up for the desk front page",
  "description": "What GET /api/projects answers since 2026-10-22. Each project row carries the record counts per surface, the newest stored timestamp, and the numbers that still need a named human. A count is null exactly when its table has never been created on this checkout, and the surface is then named in absentSurfaces: null is \"nobody has opened this here\", 0 is \"this project holds none\". The contract refuses the two readings being swapped.",
